\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\f0\fs24\cf0
\pard\plain \tx1123\tx1685\tx2246\tx2794\tx3355\tx3917\tx4478\tx5040\tx5602\tx6163\tx6725\fi720\ri-720\sl288\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We march!\u8221\'94 Pyetle shouted, and such was the force in his voice that His shout was like lifting a rock to see all the little bugs crawl, though instead of a chaos criss-crossed paths, the Vessels lined up into a three-wide column. Once settled, the hunt was on.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 It began as a hurried march up the gently rising wagon path. Mandri moved somewhere in the middle of it, wishing he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d been left behind. Two eager Hrkan Vessels made sure he was miserable. They were hard men, the type to smile but mean nothing by it; lip bite smiles, showing no teeth, a smile that says I don\u8217\'92t want know you. And they were tall. All these Vessels were tall. It must have been a requirement. The only things taller than them were the tips of their swaying spears, the red canyon walls, and Ayram, who was forced to walk somewhere near the lead. The giant was a towering black mast which frowned over all these hrkwhite heads and shoulders. It was some comfort to see him there, drifting along. It sort of gave the impression that these ignorant Hrks weren\u8217\'92t in charge, and they weren\u8217\'92t about to charge blindly into the grips of death.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 The path through the canyon branched, and the march turned left, diving into a spindly fissure where the rock curved in dramatic sweeps that towered overhead. Sunlight spilled down these sandstone fins to fill the chasm with a brilliant reddish glow. The mush of sand and fallen rock that was the floor seemed awash with cinders. Mandri kept wanting to stop and stare at warm hues he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d never seen, but he was not allowed. This was a hunt, a fact made clear by a stone brick arch which spanned the gap, and would have held a gate if the iron bars weren\u8217\'92t twisted in a heap behind it. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Beyond this gate lay the Goree\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s tallest plateau, stretching beyond vision. Cut into its eroded slope was a jagged crack. Nestled inside that shadow was an ancient stair.}
\par\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Mandri almost fainted. His aches and pains wanted nothing to do with that dizzying staircase and its thousand-something steps, each steep and uneven. They looked like a ragged line of stitches. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\pard\plain \tx1123\tx1685\tx2246\tx2794\tx3355\tx3917\tx4478\tx5040\tx5602\tx6163\tx6725\fi720\ri-720\sl288\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 The Vessel behind nudged him. He began to climb. He could not take his eyes off the stain, for it appeared it was still wet, and in places, streaming. The steps themselves were so slumped that he wondered if it wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t age that bent them, but erosion from this stream. When reached the top, he looked for the blood stain\u8217\'92s source, lifted his eyes and found himself standing at the rim of a massive crater.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Of what this was.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 A rampart of rock-splatter.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He had trouble thinking through his astonishment.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d been expecting to see a flat expanse, a sort of table for the gods, but instead he was met with a plunging hollow so expansive that the opposite bank was a few shades bluer than the slope under his feet. And that slope was vast. His sense of vertigo had never been more acute. The Hrk behind him nudged the small of his back and he nearly vomited.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 It was landscape unto itself. In the middle of it, smack-dab in the center, was a large stub of rock.}
\par\pard\plain \tx1123\tx1685\tx2246\tx2794\tx3355\tx3917\tx4478\tx5040\tx5602\tx6163\tx6725\fi720\ri-720\sl288\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Approach.}
\par\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1  And then the trail of hrkwhite cloaks, some of then already halfway down the bowl, were the size of specks. They reinvested Mandri with a sense of scale\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 absolutely enormous.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 It was a wonder.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d never seen its like.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\pard\plain \tx1123\tx1685\tx2246\tx2794\tx3355\tx3917\tx4478\tx5040\tx5602\tx6163\tx6725\fi720\ri-720\sl288\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 It was enormous, like a clay saucepot meant to feed all the sky, set upside down. It\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s rounding wall was scrawled all over with geometric designs; diamonds, squares, and circles were everywhere joined together to make abstract faces; animal faces, demonic faces, faces inside of faces. An oval taller than ten men demarcated the edges of a fox\u8217\'92s gape. The nostrils of the fox were the eyes of a hawk, and the beak of the hawk was the tooth of the fox and also the skull of a mouse. This parade of creation wrapped all the way around the pottish structure like a belt.}
\par\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Mandri had trouble thinking through his astonishment. And then the trail of hrkwhite specks climbing the structure\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s steps reinvested him with a sense of scale\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 absolutely enormous.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 It was a wonder.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d never seen its like.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 All the man-made wonders get their place in Hrkan art, and so by rights this building should have been included. The Hrkan brush is especially attracted to the monuments of Outland tribes, for the glories of the conquered vitalize the glory of the conqueror. This godly saucepot would have been a bright jewel in a Lordly crown, an especially resplendent jewel now that the evening sun painted the stone with flame. The lack of its account in Hrkan art could only be explained by ignorance\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the Lords did not know of it. If they had, the building would have been captured in a painting a long, long time ago. And the Hrks would have an easy time capturing it now, for it appeared to be abandoned. If it were a living temple, incense smoke would be everywhere smeared into the sky\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s purpling hues while dour voices chanted Old Jandri hymns with all the guttural intensity of a lizard litter brushed with the scent of a snake. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Mandri rushed along. When he stepped up the foot of the structure\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s stair and looked up, he almost fainted. His aches and pains wanted nothing to do with those three-hundred-something steps, each steep and uneven, like layers of melted wax. And worse, a dark stain climbed up them. Mandri guessed that up above, some unattended bucket of oil had spilled, found a groove, and then streamed all the way down to the bottom. If it wasn\u8217\'92t oil, well, it could be any number of other substances. Perfumed wine, red berry brine, or ink. It could be slurried excrement; a temple that large had to drain out somewhere. Odd that they\u8217\'92d have it running out the front door. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 But he knew it was blood. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Because of course it was blood.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Blood explained the stain, and it explained the general unease creeping under his skin. It explained why his knees trembled and why, as he crested the final stair and stepped onto the temple\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s forecourt, why he felt the urge to flee. And that wasn\u8217\'92t the end of it, for the curving wall\u8217\'92s innumerable faces\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 those jackals, bats, and sows\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 they all collapsed into a swirl of lines just above a yawning entrance arch, giving the impression that all the world was being sucked into the mountain. This was a carnivorous beast. Most of those swirling faces were stained by that same dark substance which dripped down the stairs. Yes, that grand entrance arch was a blood-stained maw. Perhaps it had eaten the Greskalun. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 More explanatory power.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Form up!\u8221\'94 Pyetle barked, his voice a little slimmer in this thinner air.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 A Vessel grabbed Mandri by the neck and arranged him alongside the assembling Hrkan squares. When they were all formed up atop that table of rock, Pyetle began a formal review. }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 His stern eye ticked from face to face. He seemed upset. }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Mandri risked a sheepish glance to try and puzzle out what was fouling Pyetle\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s mood, and of course, there was Elrahet, a hunched rock of a woman in this sea of hrkwhite robes. She and Pyetle stared each other down in some arcane contest of wills.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Sir!\u8221\'94 A Vessel shouted. \u8220\'93There is someone inside!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Pyetle spun around and hurried to the temple\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s blood-stained threshold. He drew his sword as if to do battle with the building, then peered inside its mouth. After a wary inspection, he shouted, \u8220\'93A torch!\u8221\'94}}